        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Incline walking works the glutes harder than flat walking, but
            it is an endurance stimulus, not a glute-building programme.</strong> Beginners and
            deconditioned people may gain some strength from it; anyone wanting noticeably
            stronger or bigger glutes needs progressive resistance training alongside it.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Walk at the commonly suggested 8 to 12% once you have built up to it, stand tall, take a
            full stride and let go of the rails, and give the strength work its own sessions. For
